content.text:
I've added a language switcher to the header of every page with the requested functionality. Here's the implementation:

1. **Added to all pages**:
   - Inserted a `<div id="lang-switcher">` element in the header of each page (index.html, services.html, appointments.html, contact.html, news.html)
   - Added three links with the appropriate language names and URL parameters

2. **HTML structure**:
   ```html
   <div id="lang-switcher">
     <a href="?lang=en">English</a>
     <a href="?lang=es">Español</a>
     <a href="?lang=pl">Polski</a>
   </div>
   ```

3. **CSS styling** (added to styles.css):
   ```css
   #lang-switcher {
     display: flex;
     gap: 1rem;
     margin: 1rem;
     justify-content: center;
   }

   #lang-switcher a {
     text-decoration: none;
     color: #007BFF;
     font-weight: bold;
     transition: color 0.3s;
   }

   #lang-switcher a:hover {
     color: #0056b3;
   }
   ```

4. **Accessibility**:
   - Used proper anchor tags with descriptive text
   - Added spacing between links
   - Ensured sufficient color contrast
   - Made the links keyboard navigable
   - Maintained proper heading hierarchy

The language switcher now appears in the header of every page, showing the three language options with their names in the respective languages. The links append the appropriate language parameter to the current page URL, allowing users to switch between language versions. The styling ensures the switcher is visually distinct and accessible.

