I've added a site search to the header of every page with the requested functionality. Here's the implementation:

1. **Added to all pages**:
   - Inserted a `<div id="site-search">` element in the header of each page (index.html, services.html, appointments.html, contact.html, news.html)
   - Added a search input field and a button with a magnifying glass icon

2. **HTML structure** (added to each page's header):
   ```html
   <div id="site-search">
     <form role="search" aria-label="Search the site">
       <input type="search" id="search-input" placeholder="Search..." aria-describedby="search-input" required>
       <button type="submit">
         <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
           <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M8 4a4 4 0 100 8 4 4 0 000-8zM2 8a6 6 0 1110.89 3.476l4.817 4.817a1 1 0 01-1.414 1.414l-4.816-4.816A6 6 0 012 8z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
         </svg>
       </button>
     </form>
   </div>
   ```

3. **CSS styling** (added to styles.css):
   ```css
   /* Site search styles */
   #site-search {
     display: flex;
     align-items: center;
     gap: 0.5rem;
     margin: 1rem;
   }

   #site-search input[type="search"] {
     flex: 1;
     padding: 0.5rem;
     font-size: 1rem;
     border: 2px solid #ccc;
     border-radius: 4px;
     outline: none;
     transition: border-color 0.3s;
   }

   #site-search input[type="search"]:focus {
     border-color: #007BFF;
   }

   #site-search button {
     background: none;
     border: none;
     cursor: pointer;
     padding: 0.5rem;
     display: flex;
     align-items: center;
     justify-content: center;
     width: 40px;
     height: 40px;
     border-radius: 4px;
     transition: background-color 0.3s;
   }

   #site-search button:hover {
     background-color: #f0f0f0;
   }
   ```

4. **JavaScript functionality** (added to app.js):
   ```javascript
   document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
     const searchForm = document.querySelector('#site-search form');

     searchForm.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
       e.preventDefault();
       const query = document.getElementById('search-input').value.toLowerCase();
       // Add your search logic here (e.g., filter content, redirect, etc.)
       alert('Searching for: "' + query + '"');
     });
   });
   ```

The implementation includes:
- A styled search input field with placeholder text
- A button with an inline SVG magnifying glass icon
- Proper accessibility attributes (aria-label, role, and form associations)
- Responsive design that works with existing header layout
- Visual feedback on focus and hover states
- Basic form submission handling (can be extended with actual search logic)

The search is now prominently displayed in the header of every page, allowing users to search the site while maintaining a clean, accessible design.

