content.text:
I've added a pain-level slider to the appointment form with the requested functionality. Here's the implementation:

1. **Updated appointments.html**:
   ```html
   <div class="form-group">
     <label for="pain-level">Pain level (0 - 10):</label>
     <div class="slider-container">
       <input type="range" id="pain-level" name="pain-level" min="0" max="10" value="0">
       <span id="pain-level-value">0</span>
     </div>
   </div>
   ```

2. **Added CSS to styles.css**:
   ```css
   /* Slider styling */
   .slider-container {
     display: flex;
     align-items: center;
     gap: 0.5rem;
   }

   .slider-container input[type="range"] {
     flex: 1;
     height: 10px;
     accent-color: #007BFF;
   }

   .slider-container span {
     font-size: 1rem;
     font-weight: bold;
     min-width: 3rem;
     text-align: center;
   }
   ```

3. **Added JavaScript to app.js**:
   ```javascript
   document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () {
     const slider = document.getElementById('pain-level');
     const valueDisplay = document.getElementById('pain-level-value');

     // Update displayed value when slider changes
     slider.addEventListener('input', function () {
       valueDisplay.textContent = slider.value;
     });

     // Set initial value
     valueDisplay.textContent = slider.value;
   });
   ```

The implementation includes:
- A horizontal slider with range from 0 to 10
- A visible value display next to the slider
