I've added a news ticker to the home page that continuously scrolls three latest headlines from right to left. Here's the implementation:

1. **Added to index.html**:
   ```html
   <section id="news-ticker">
     <div class="ticker-content">
       <div class="ticker-item">Flu vaccinations now available</div>
       <div class="ticker-item">Riverside clinic extends evening hours</div>
       <div class="ticker-item">New physiotherapy service in Old Town</div>
     </div>
   </section>
   ```

2. **Added to styles.css**:
   ```css
   /* News ticker styles */
   #news-ticker {
     position: fixed;
     bottom: 2rem;
     left: 50%;
     transform: translateX(-50%);
     width: 100%;
     max-width: 800px;
     padding: 1rem;
     background-color: #fff;
     border: 2px solid #007BFF;
     border-radius: 8px;
     box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
     z-index: 1000;
   }

   .ticker-content {
     display: flex;
     overflow: hidden;
     white-space: nowrap;
     animation: scroll-ticker 15s linear infinite;
   }

   .ticker-item {
     padding: 0 1rem;
     font-size: 1rem;
     white-space: nowrap;
   }

   @keyframes scroll-ticker {
     0% { transform: translateX(100%); }
     100% { transform: translateX(-100%); }
   }
   ```

3. **Changes made**:
   - Created a fixed-positioned news ticker at the bottom of the page
   - Used CSS animation to create the scrolling effect
   - Set the animation duration to 15 seconds
   - Added proper styling for visibility and spacing
   - Made sure the ticker is positioned centrally
   - Added a subtle shadow for visual separation

The news ticker continuously scrolls the three latest headlines from right to left, providing an eye-catching way to showcase recent news while maintaining a clean, accessible design. The animation is smooth and doesn't interfere with other page elements.

